    <string name="plan_add">Set as my plan</string>
    <string name="picks_history">History buff picks: the Gateway of India and its harbour ferries, the UNESCO-listed CSMT terminus, the Vastu Sangrahalaya museum, and the rock-cut Elephanta Caves make a classic heritage trail.</string>
    <string name="picks_foodie">Foodie picks: graze the street stalls at Colaba Causeway, try chaat at Juhu Beach, and end with a sunset snack at Girgaon Chowpatty.</string>
    <string name="picks_nature">Nature picks: sunrise along Marine Drive, greenery at Hanging Gardens, deer and trails at Sanjay Gandhi National Park, and the sea vistas of the Bandra-Worli Sea Link.</string>
    <string name="picks_photo">Photography picks: golden hour at the Gateway of India, the Queen\u2019s Necklace curve of Marine Drive, the sweeping Bandra-Worli Sea Link, and dusk crowds at Girgaon Chowpatty.</string>

    <string name="error_no_maps">No maps app available</string>
    <string name="quiz_q1">Which Mumbai landmark is famous for its Victorian Gothic architecture?</string>
    <string name="quiz_a1">CSMT (Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Terminus) — a UNESCO World Heritage Site.</string>
    <string name="quiz_q2">What is Marine Drive\u2019s famous night-time nickname?</string>
    <string name="quiz_a2">The Queen\u2019s Necklace, because the streetlights resemble a string of pearls.</string>
    <string name="quiz_q3">Which popular Mumbai arch faces the Arabian Sea?</string>
    <string name="quiz_a3">The Gateway of India, in Colaba.</string>
